/-!
# The generated local Spin Maurer lift

Finite Spin and Lorentz identities are differentiated on the point-normalized
field generated by one primitive local `SL(2,C)` field.  The resulting right
Maurer Lorentz connection is Lorentz-skew and its fixed Clifford lift is the
right Maurer derivative of the actual Dirac representation.

No `dS`, `dR`, Maurer matrix, connection, skewness, lift, or covariance
certificate is accepted independently.  This is the missing inhomogeneous
leg needed to combine the already proved finite homogeneous lift covariance
with the actual local matter product rule.
-/

namespace
  SaturationMonoid.PhysicsCore.StageNineDiracKineticLocalSpinMaurerLift

open DiracCliffordRepresentation
open PointwiseDiracSpinConnectionLift
open ProofFreeRicherAnholonomicSource
open StageNineDiracGammaCentralizer
